Ladybird now resolves the Auto contrast preference from the preference
Qt reports, which on macOS is NSWorkspace’s Increase Contrast setting,
accessibilityDisplayShouldIncreaseContrast, and on Linux the settings
portal’s org.freedesktop.appearance contrast. On macOS, Blink, Gecko and
WebKit report more for the same setting (OsSettingsProviderMac::
PreferredContrast(), nsLookAndFeel::NativeGetInt() for the accessibility
theme, ThemeMac::userPreferredContrast()), and follow it through
NSWorkspaceAccessibilityDisplayOptionsDidChangeNotification. On Linux,
Gecko also reports more for a portal contrast of 1 (nsLookAndFeel::
RecomputeDBusAppearanceSetting()), while Blink looks only at the names
of GTK themes. Read from source, not run: Chromium e6c8d7c15aeb2,
Firefox 41db707342fe, WebKit c3a7f3c0cfe0.
